// MENUDEF - the mod's own menu. ZDoom wiki: https://zdoom.org/wiki/MENUDEF
//
// A MENUDEF lump does not replace GZDoom's menus; it adds to them. The two
// directives used here:
//
//   OptionMenu "<name>"       declares a new menu screen.
//   AddOptionMenu "<name>"    APPENDS items to a menu that already exists,
//                             leaving the rest of the engine's menu intact.
//                             (GZDoom's own option menus are declared
//                             `protected`, which forbids a mod from adding
//                             Command/SafeCommand items - arbitrary console
//                             commands - but allows Submenu, Option and
//                             StaticText. Verified in-engine 2026-10-13.)
//
// WHY THERE IS NO CVAR OF OUR OWN FOR THE LANGUAGE.
// GZDoom already ships the `language` CVar, and it is archived: the engine
// writes it to the player's gzdoom.ini and reads it back next launch. That
// is exactly the persistence the CEO asked for, in the place a player
// expects their settings to live, and it is the ONLY key this mod ever
// touches in their config. A mod-owned CVar would be a second source of
// truth and a second thing written to their file.
// See docs/engine/adr/004-difficulty-ladder-and-language-switch.md.

// The two values the mod supports, and nothing else: the CEO asked for an
// explicit choice, not for the system locale to decide. "default" is
// GZDoom's code for the LANGUAGE section marked `default` (ours is
// `[enu default]`); "ru" selects `[ru]`.
//
// The labels are localized like everything else, so the Russian build names
// the languages in Russian. They are NOT endonyms ("Русский" inside the
// English menu) because Freedoom's font cannot draw Cyrillic yet and the
// entry would read as blank - debt T9.
OptionValue "SD_LanguageValues"
{
	"default", "$SD_LANGVAL_EN"
	"ru",      "$SD_LANGVAL_RU"
}

OptionMenu "SD_OptionsMenu"
{
	Title "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE"
	Option "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGUAGE", "language", "SD_LanguageValues"
	StaticText " "
	StaticText "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGHELP"
	// Temporary while debt T9 (the Cyrillic font) is open. Delete this line
	// and its LANGUAGE ids in the same change that lands the glyphs.
	StaticText "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGWARN"
}

AddOptionMenu "OptionsMenu"
{
	StaticText " "
	Submenu "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE", "SD_OptionsMenu"
}
